            <div xml:id="d605">

                <pb facs="0902" n="766" xml:id="pg766"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">723.2515/3321: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Peru</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Moore</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-04-11T17:00:00-05:00">April 11, 1929—5
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>44. Your 55, March 31, 4 p.m., eighth paragraph. In your discretion you may
                    communicate the following orally and confidentially to President Leguia. When
                    the time comes, President Hoover is ready to make a suggestion of settlement to
                    both Peru and Chile on the condition that the settlement which the President is
                    to suggest has the prior approval of both Peru and Chile.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
